if you wear glasses you know wearing a  mask can be pretty annoying  the lenses will fog up the straps behind  your ears kind of become uncomfortable  well now some people are turning to  surgery during the pandemic for a fix  [Applause]  a relatively new form of eye surgery for  people who want to stop wearing glasses  or contacts  is gaining popularity in maryland during  the pandemic  it's called smile laser eye surgery and  smile is short for a small incision  lenticular extraction  dr sonny goal says smile is an  alternative to lasik  it was approved by the fda in 2016.  think of it as like small incision lasik  we're able to treat a patient without  making a large corneal flap  just making a very small four millimeter  incision up under the upper eyelid  glasses um especially with masks now  um fogging up constantly and just  so uncomfortable um on the back of the  ears with the mask and stuff  and so i just thought i've been thinking  about this for so  long it's time to just do it melissa  nelson recently had the surgery which  doctors say is less invasive and  patients recover faster  by the next day i was able to drive  wear eye makeup rub my eyes like other  eye surgery there is a risk of  complications  that includes glare and halos  particularly at night  also debris where the corneal disc was  removed inflammation and infection is  all possible  but despite the risks dr gold says his  patients have been very happy with the  surgery's results  this has just been a game changer for  them i mean they've been really  impressed by how quick and easy the  procedure is  research has shown that smile also  results in less dry eye symptoms than  lasik
 

